    "embedding_text": "Archive via Utility (T1560.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. Adversaries may use utilities to compress and/or encrypt collected data prior to exfiltration. Many utilities include functionalities to compress, encrypt, or otherwise package data into a format that is easier/more secure to transport.\n\nAdversaries may abuse various utilities to compress or encrypt data before exfiltration. Some third party utilities may be preinstalled, such as <code>tar</code> on Linux and macOS or <code>zip</code> on Windows systems. \n\nOn Windows, <code>diantz</code> or <cod It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT1, APT28, APT3, APT33, APT39, APT41, APT5, Agrius and malware families such as AppleSeed, BeaverTail, CORALDECK, Calisto, Crutch, Daserf, DustySky, GlassWorm. Recommended mitigations include Audit. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Creation, Module Load, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may use utilities to compress and/or encrypt collected data prior to exfiltration.",
