    "embedding_text": "Windows Management Instrumentation (T1047) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Execution tactic. Adversaries may abuse Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI) to execute malicious commands and payloads. WMI is designed for programmers and is the infrastructure for management data and operations on Windows systems.(Citation: WMI 1-3) WMI is an administration feature that provides a uniform environment to access Windows system components.\n\nThe WMI service enables both local and remote access, though the latter is facilitated by [Remote Services](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1021) suc It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT-C-36, APT29, APT32, APT41, APT42, Aquatic Panda, BlackByte, Blue Mockingbird and malware families such as Action RAT, Agent Tesla, Akira, AshTag, Astaroth, Avaddon, BADHATCH, Bazar. Recommended mitigations include Privileged Account Management, Behavior Prevention on Endpoint, User Account Management, Execution Prevention. Detection relies on Network Connection Creation, Process Creation, WMI Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may abuse Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI) to execute malicious commands and payloads.",
