    "embedding_text": "Exploitation for Defense Impairment (T1687) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Defense Impairment tactic. Adversaries may exploit vulnerabilities in security software, infrastructure, or defensive components to degrade, disable, or otherwise continue to impair their ability to prevent, detect, or respond to malicious activity. \n \nAdversaries may exploit a system or application vulnerability to directly interfere with defensive mechanisms. Exploitation occurs when an adversary takes advantage of a programming error in software, services, or the operating system to execute adversary-controlled code, o It affects IaaS, Linux, macOS, SaaS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors . Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Application Log Content, Cloud Service Disable, Command Execution, Driver Load, Driver Metadata.",
