    "embedding_text": "Screen Capture (T1113) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. Adversaries may attempt to take screen captures of the desktop to gather information over the course of an operation. Screen capturing functionality may be included as a feature of a remote access tool used in post-compromise operations. Taking a screenshot is also typically possible through native utilities or API calls, such as <code>CopyFromScreen</code>, <code>xwd</code>, or <code>screencapture</code>.(Citation: CopyFromScreen .NET)(Citation: Antiquated Mac Malware)\n It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, APT39, APT42, BRONZE BUTLER, Dark Caracal, Dragonfly, FIN7, GOLD SOUTHFIELD and malware families such as Agent Tesla, AppleSeed, Aria-body, AshTag, Attor, Azorult, BADHATCH, BADNEWS. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Module Load, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may attempt to take screen captures of the desktop to gather information over the course of an operation.",
