    "embedding_text": "OS Credential Dumping (T1003) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Credential Access tactic. Adversaries may attempt to dump credentials to obtain account login and credential material, normally in the form of a hash or a clear text password. Credentials can be obtained from OS caches, memory, or structures.(Citation: Brining MimiKatz to Unix) Credentials can then be used to perform [Lateral Movement](https://attack.mitre.org/tactics/TA0008) and access restricted information.\n\nSeveral of the tools mentioned in associated sub-techniques may be used by both adversaries and professional se It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, APT32, APT39, Axiom, BlackByte, Ember Bear, Leviathan, Mustang Panda and malware families such as Carbanak, HOMEFRY, MgBot, OnionDuke, PinchDuke, Revenge RAT, Trojan.Karagany. Recommended mitigations include Encrypt Sensitive Information, Behavior Prevention on Endpoint, Password Policies, User Training, Privileged Account Management. Detection relies on Active Directory Object Access, File Access, Process Access, Process Creation, Process Metadata.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may attempt to dump credentials to obtain account login and credential material, normally in the form of a hash or a clear text password.",
