    "embedding_text": "Rootkit (T1014) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may use rootkits to hide the presence of programs, files, network connections, services, drivers, and other system components. Rootkits are programs that hide the existence of malware by intercepting/hooking and modifying operating system API calls that supply system information. (Citation: Symantec Windows Rootkits) \n\nRootkits or rootkit enabling functionality may reside at the user or kernel level in the operating system or lower, to include a hypervisor or [System Firmware](https: It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, APT41, Rocke, TeamTNT, UNC3886, Winnti Group and malware families such as COATHANGER, Carberp, Caterpillar WebShell, Drovorub, Ebury, HIDEDRV, Hacking Team UEFI Rootkit, HiddenWasp. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Driver Load, File Creation, File Modification, Module Load, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may use rootkits to hide the presence of programs, files, network connections, services, drivers, and other system components.",
