    "embedding_text": "Bypass User Account Control (T1548.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Privilege Escalation tactic. Adversaries may bypass UAC mechanisms to elevate process privileges on system. Windows User Account Control (UAC) allows a program to elevate its privileges (tracked as integrity levels ranging from low to high) to perform a task under administrator-level permissions, possibly by prompting the user for confirmation. The impact to the user ranges from denying the operation under high enforcement to allowing the user to perform the action if they are in the local administrators group and click thr It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT29, APT37, APT38, BRONZE BUTLER, Cobalt Group, Earth Lusca, Evilnum, Medusa Group and malware families such as AppleJeus, AutoIt backdoor, Avaddon, BADHATCH, Bad Rabbit, BitPaymer, BlackCat, BlackEnergy. Recommended mitigations include Update Software, Audit, User Account Control, Privileged Account Management. Detection relies on Logon Session Metadata, Module Load, Process Access, Process Creation, Windows Registry Key Modification.",
