    "embedding_text": "Permission Groups Discovery (T1069) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Discovery tactic. Adversaries may attempt to discover group and permission settings. This information can help adversaries determine which user accounts and groups are available, the membership of users in particular groups, and which users and groups have elevated permissions.\n\nAdversaries may attempt to discover group permission settings in many different ways. This data may provide the adversary with information about the compromised environment that can be used in follow-on activity and targeting.(Citation: C It affects Containers, IaaS, Identity Provider, Linux, macOS, Office Suite, SaaS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT3, APT41, FIN13, Scattered Spider, TA505, Volt Typhoon and malware families such as Carbon, IcedID, MURKYTOP, Siloscape, TrickBot. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Command Execution, Process Creation.",
