    "embedding_text": "Email Collection (T1114) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. Adversaries may target user email to collect sensitive information. Emails may contain sensitive data, including trade secrets or personal information, that can prove valuable to adversaries. Emails may also contain details of ongoing incident response operations, which may allow adversaries to adjust their techniques in order to maintain persistence or evade defenses.(Citation: TrustedSec OOB Communications)(Citation: CISA AA20-352A 2021) Adversaries can collect or forward email from mail serve It affects Windows, macOS, Linux, Office Suite platforms and has been observed used by Ember Bear, Magic Hound, Scattered Spider, Silent Librarian and malware families such as Emotet, TRANSLATEXT. Recommended mitigations include Multi-factor Authentication, Out-of-Band Communications Channel, Encrypt Sensitive Information, Audit. Detection relies on Application Log Content, Command Execution, File Access, Logon Session Creation, Network Connection Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may target user email to collect sensitive information.",
