    "embedding_text": "Security Account Manager (T1003.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Credential Access tactic. Adversaries may attempt to extract credential material from the Security Account Manager (SAM) database either through in-memory techniques or through the Windows Registry where the SAM database is stored. The SAM is a database file that contains local accounts for the host, typically those found with the <code>net user</code> command. Enumerating the SAM database requires SYSTEM level access.\n\nA number of tools can be used to retrieve the SAM file through in-memory techniques:\n\n* pwdumpx.exe\n*  It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT29, APT41, APT5, Agrius, Daggerfly, Dragonfly, Ember Bear, FIN13 and malware families such as Cobalt Strike, CosmicDuke, CozyCar, HOPLIGHT, IceApple, Mivast, POWERTON, Remsec. Recommended mitigations include Password Policies, Privileged Account Management, Operating System Configuration, User Training. Detection relies on File Creation, File Modification, Process Creation, Windows Registry Key Modification.",
