    "embedding_text": "Application Exhaustion Flood (T1499.003) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Impact tactic. Adversaries may target resource intensive features of applications to cause a denial of service (DoS), denying availability to those applications. For example, specific features in web applications may be highly resource intensive. Repeated requests to those features may be able to exhaust system resources and deny access to the application or the server itself.(Citation: Arbor AnnualDoSreport Jan 2018) It affects Windows, IaaS, Linux, macOS platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors . Recommended mitigations include Filter Network Traffic. Detection relies on Application Log Content, Cloud Service Metadata, Host Status, Network Traffic Content, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may target resource intensive features of applications to cause a denial of service (DoS), denying availability to those applications.",
