    "embedding_text": "Bootkit (T1542.003) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth, Persistence tactic. Adversaries may use bootkits to persist on systems. A bootkit is a malware variant that modifies the boot sectors of a hard drive, allowing malicious code to execute before a computer's operating system has loaded. Bootkits reside at a layer below the operating system and may make it difficult to perform full remediation unless an organization suspects one was used and can act accordingly.\n\nIn BIOS systems, a bootkit may modify the Master Boot Record (MBR) and/or Volume Boot Record (VBR).(Citati It affects Linux, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, APT41, Lazarus Group and malware families such as BOOTRASH, Carberp, FinFisher, ROCKBOOT, TrickBot, WhisperGate. Recommended mitigations include Boot Integrity, Privileged Account Management. Detection relies on Drive Access, Drive Modification, File Creation, File Modification.",
