    "beginner_explanation": "Data from Removable Media is a technique attackers use during the Collection stage of an intrusion. In simple terms: Adversaries may search connected removable media on computers they have compromised to find files of interest.",
    "analyst_explanation": "Adversaries may search connected removable media on computers they have compromised to find files of interest. Sensitive data can be collected from any removable media (optical disk drive, USB memory, etc.) connected to the compromised system prior to Exfiltration. Interactive command shells may be in use, and common functionality within [cmd](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0106) may be used to gather information. \n\nSome adversaries may also use [Automated Collection](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1119) on removable media.",
    "executive_summary": "Data from Removable Media (T1025) is a medium-severity technique observed in real-world use by 24 known threat actor(s)/malware families, primarily impacting Linux, macOS, Windows.",
