    "embedding_text": "Data from Removable Media (T1025) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. Adversaries may search connected removable media on computers they have compromised to find files of interest. Sensitive data can be collected from any removable media (optical disk drive, USB memory, etc.) connected to the compromised system prior to Exfiltration. Interactive command shells may be in use, and common functionality within [cmd](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0106) may be used to gather information. \n\nSome adversaries may also use [Automated Collection](https://attack.mitre.or It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, Gamaredon Group, OilRig, Turla and malware families such as AppleSeed, Aria-body, BADNEWS, CosmicDuke, Crimson, Crutch, Explosive, FLASHFLOOD. Recommended mitigations include Data Loss Prevention. Detection relies on Drive Creation, File Access, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may search connected removable media on computers they have compromised to find files of interest.",
