    "embedding_text": "Local Data Staging (T1074.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. Adversaries may stage collected data in a central location or directory on the local system prior to Exfiltration. Data may be kept in separate files or combined into one file through techniques such as [Archive Collected Data](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1560). Interactive command shells may be used, and common functionality within [cmd](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0106) and bash may be used to copy data into a staging location.\n\nAdversaries may also stage collected data in vari It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, APT3, APT39, APT5, Agrius, BackdoorDiplomacy, Chimera, Dragonfly and malware families such as ADVSTORESHELL, AppleSeed, Astaroth, Attor, AuTo Stealer, BADNEWS, BadPatch, BeaverTail. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Access, File Creation, Process Creation, Snapshot Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may stage collected data in a central location or directory on the local system prior to Exfiltration.",
