    "embedding_text": "Stored Data Manipulation (T1565.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Impact tactic. Adversaries may insert, delete, or manipulate data at rest in order to influence external outcomes or hide activity, thus threatening the integrity of the data.(Citation: FireEye APT38 Oct 2018)(Citation: DOJ Lazarus Sony 2018) By manipulating stored data, adversaries may attempt to affect a business process, organizational understanding, and decision making.\n\nStored data could include a variety of file formats, such as Office files, databases, stored emails, and custom file formats. The type of It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT38 and malware families such as MultiLayer Wiper, SUNSPOT. Recommended mitigations include Restrict File and Directory Permissions, Remote Data Storage, Encrypt Sensitive Information. Detection relies on File Creation, File Deletion, File Metadata, File Modification.",
