    "embedding_text": "Password Cracking (T1110.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Credential Access tactic. Adversaries may use password cracking to attempt to recover usable credentials, such as plaintext passwords, when credential material such as password hashes are obtained. [OS Credential Dumping](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1003) can be used to obtain password hashes, this may only get an adversary so far when [Pass the Hash](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1550/002) is not an option. Further,  adversaries may leverage [Data from Configuration Repository](https://attack.mitre.org/t It affects Identity Provider, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Office Suite, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT3, Dragonfly, FIN6, Salt Typhoon and malware families such as Net Crawler. Recommended mitigations include Password Policies, Multi-factor Authentication. Detection relies on File Access, File Creation, Process Access, Process Creation, User Account Authentication.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may use password cracking to attempt to recover usable credentials, such as plaintext passwords, when credential material such as password hashes are obtained.",
