    "embedding_text": "Hide Artifacts (T1564) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may attempt to hide artifacts associated with their behaviors to evade detection. Operating systems may have features to hide various artifacts, such as important system files and administrative task execution, to avoid disrupting user work environments and prevent users from changing files or features on the system. Adversaries may abuse these features to hide artifacts such as files, directories, user accounts, or other system activity to evade detection.(Citation: Sofacy Komplex T It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Office Suite, Windows platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors and malware families such as Bundlore, DarkTortilla, NOOPLDR, OSX/Shlayer, Tarrask, WarzoneRAT. Recommended mitigations include Limit Software Installation, Application Developer Guidance, Audit, Antivirus/Antimalware. Detection relies on Application Log Content, Command Execution, File Creation, File Metadata, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may attempt to hide artifacts associated with their behaviors to evade detection.",
