    "beginner_explanation": "Domain Groups is a technique attackers use during the Discovery stage of an intrusion. In simple terms: Adversaries may attempt to find domain-level groups and permission settings.",
    "analyst_explanation": "Adversaries may attempt to find domain-level groups and permission settings. The knowledge of domain-level permission groups can help adversaries determine which groups exist and which users belong to a particular group. Adversaries may use this information to determine which users have elevated permissions, such as domain administrators.\n\nCommands such as <code>net group /domain</code> of the [Net](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0039) utility,  <code>dscacheutil -q group</code> on macOS, and <code>ldapsearch</code> on Linux can list domain-level groups.",
