    "embedding_text": "Domain Groups (T1069.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Discovery tactic. Adversaries may attempt to find domain-level groups and permission settings. The knowledge of domain-level permission groups can help adversaries determine which groups exist and which users belong to a particular group. Adversaries may use this information to determine which users have elevated permissions, such as domain administrators.\n\nCommands such as <code>net group /domain</code> of the [Net](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0039) utility,  <code>dscacheutil -q group</code> on macOS, an It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by Dragonfly, FIN7, INC Ransom, Inception, Ke3chang, LAPSUS$, Medusa Group, Mustang Panda and malware families such as BADHATCH, BlackCat, Cobalt Strike, Egregor, GRIFFON, Gootloader, Helminth, Kwampirs. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Command Execution, Network Traffic Content, Process Creation.",
