    "embedding_text": "SSH (T1021.004) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Lateral Movement tactic. Adversaries may use [Valid Accounts](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1078) to log into remote machines using Secure Shell (SSH). The adversary may then perform actions as the logged-on user.\n\nSSH is a protocol that allows authorized users to open remote shells on other computers. Many Linux and macOS versions come with SSH installed by default, although typically disabled until the user enables it. On ESXi, SSH can be enabled either directly on the host (e.g., via `vim-cmd hostsvc/enable_ss It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS platforms and has been observed used by APT39, APT5, Aquatic Panda, BlackTech, FIN13, FIN7, Fox Kitten, GCMAN and malware families such as Cobalt Strike, Kinsing, Qilin, reGeorg. Recommended mitigations include Disable or Remove Feature or Program, Multi-factor Authentication, User Account Management. Detection relies on Command Execution, Logon Session Creation, Logon Session Metadata, Network Traffic Content, Network Traffic Flow.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may use [Valid Accounts](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1078) to log into remote machines using Secure Shell (SSH).",
