    "embedding_text": "Component Object Model (T1559.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Execution tactic. Adversaries may use the Windows Component Object Model (COM) for local code execution. COM is an inter-process communication (IPC) component of the native Windows application programming interface (API) that enables interaction between software objects, or executable code that implements one or more interfaces.(Citation: Fireeye Hunting COM June 2019) Through COM, a client object can call methods of server objects, which are typically binary Dynamic Link Libraries (DLL) or executables (EXE).(Cit It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by Gamaredon Group, Kimsuky, Medusa Group, MuddyWater and malware families such as Bumblebee, CLAIMLOADER, DarkTortilla, FunnyDream, Gelsemium, HermeticWizard, InvisiMole, Latrodectus. Recommended mitigations include Privileged Account Management, Application Isolation and Sandboxing. Detection relies on Module Load, Process Creation, Windows Registry Key Access.",
