    "embedding_text": "Automated Collection (T1119) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. Once established within a system or network, an adversary may use automated techniques for collecting internal data. Methods for performing this technique could include use of a [Command and Scripting Interpreter](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059) to search for and copy information fitting set criteria such as file type, location, or name at specific time intervals. \n\nIn cloud-based environments, adversaries may also use cloud APIs, data pipelines, command line interfaces, or extract, t It affects IaaS, Linux, macOS, Office Suite, SaaS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT1, APT28, Agrius, Chimera, Confucius, Ember Bear, FIN5, FIN6 and malware families such as AppleSeed, Attor, BADNEWS, Bankshot, Comnie, Crutch, DarkGate, FunnyDream. Recommended mitigations include Remote Data Storage, Encrypt Sensitive Information. Detection relies on File Access, File Creation, Process Creation, Script Execution, User Account Authentication.",
    "semantic_summary": "Once established within a system or network, an adversary may use automated techniques for collecting internal data.",
