    "embedding_text": "System Service Discovery (T1007) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Discovery tactic. Adversaries may try to gather information about registered local system services. Adversaries may obtain information about services using tools as well as OS utility commands such as <code>sc query</code>, <code>tasklist /svc</code>, <code>systemctl --type=service</code>, and <code>net start</code>. Adversaries may also gather information about schedule tasks via commands such as `schtasks` on Windows or `crontab -l` on Linux and macOS.(Citation: Elastic Security Labs GOSAR 2024)(Citation: Senti It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT1, Aquatic Panda, BRONZE BUTLER, Chimera, Earth Lusca, Indrik Spider, Ke3chang, Kimsuky and malware families such as BBSRAT, Babuk, BitPaymer, Black Basta, Caterpillar WebShell, Cobalt Strike, Comnie, Cuba. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Command Execution, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may try to gather information about registered local system services.",
