    "embedding_text": "Peripheral Device Discovery (T1120) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Discovery tactic. Adversaries may attempt to gather information about attached peripheral devices and components connected to a computer system.(Citation: Peripheral Discovery Linux)(Citation: Peripheral Discovery macOS) Peripheral devices could include auxiliary resources that support a variety of functionalities such as keyboards, printers, cameras, smart card readers, or removable storage. The information may be used to enhance their awareness of the system and network environment or may be used for further ac It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, APT37, BackdoorDiplomacy, Equation, Gamaredon Group, OilRig, TeamTNT, Turla and malware families such as ADVSTORESHELL, AcidPour, Attor, BADNEWS, Bandook, BlackEnergy, CHIMNEYSWEEP, Cadelspy. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Drive Access, File Access, Process Access, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may attempt to gather information about attached peripheral devices and components connected to a computer system.(Citation: Peripheral Discovery Linux)(Citation: Peripheral Discovery macOS) Peripheral devices could include auxiliary resources that support a variety of functionalities such as keyboards, printers, cameras, smart card readers, or removable storage.",
