    "embedding_text": "Disable or Modify Cloud Log (T1685.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Defense Impairment tactic. An adversary may disable or modify cloud logging capabilities and integrations to limit what data is collected on their activities and avoid detection. Cloud environments allow for collection and analysis of audit and application logs that provide insight into what activities a user does within the environment. If an adversary has sufficient permissions, they can disable or modify logging to avoid detection of their activities. \n\nFor example, in AWS an adversary may disable CloudWatch/CloudTrail It affects IaaS, SaaS, Identity Provider, Office Suite platforms and has been observed used by APT29 . Recommended mitigations include User Account Management. Detection relies on Cloud Service Disable, Cloud Service Modification, User Account Modification.",
