    "embedding_text": "Network Trust Dependencies (T1590.003) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Reconnaissance tactic. Adversaries may gather information about the victim's network trust dependencies that can be used during targeting. Information about network trusts may include a variety of details, including second or third-party organizations/domains (ex: managed service providers, contractors, etc.) that have connected (and potentially elevated) network access.\n\nAdversaries may gather this information in various ways, such as direct elicitation via [Phishing for Information](https://attack.mitre.org/techniqu It affects PRE platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors . Recommended mitigations include Pre-compromise. Detection relies on behavioral monitoring.",
