    "beginner_explanation": "Data from Local System is a technique attackers use during the Collection stage of an intrusion. In simple terms: Adversaries may search local system sources, such as file systems, configuration files, local databases, virtual machine files, or process memory, to find files of interest and sensitive data prior to Exfiltration.",
    "analyst_explanation": "Adversaries may search local system sources, such as file systems, configuration files, local databases, virtual machine files, or process memory, to find files of interest and sensitive data prior to Exfiltration.\n\nAdversaries may do this using a [Command and Scripting Interpreter](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059), such as [cmd](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0106) as well as a [Network Device CLI](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/008), which have functionality to interact with the file system to gather information.(Citation: show_run_config_cmd_cisco) Adversaries may a",
    "executive_summary": "Data from Local System (T1005) is a medium-severity technique observed in real-world use by 202 known threat actor(s)/malware families, primarily impacting ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows.",
    "attacker_view": "An attacker leverages Data from Local System to advance the 'Collection' objective, typically requiring access to a ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows system.",
    "defender_view": "Defenders should monitor Command Execution, File Access, File Creation and apply mitigations such as Data Loss Prevention to reduce exposure to Data from Local System.",
    "detection_story": "This technique can be surfaced by correlating Detection of Local Data Collection Prior to Exfiltration.",
