    "embedding_text": "Data from Local System (T1005) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. Adversaries may search local system sources, such as file systems, configuration files, local databases, virtual machine files, or process memory, to find files of interest and sensitive data prior to Exfiltration.\n\nAdversaries may do this using a [Command and Scripting Interpreter](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059), such as [cmd](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0106) as well as a [Network Device CLI](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/008), which have functionality to interac It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT1, APT28, APT29, APT3, APT37, APT38, APT39, APT41 and malware families such as Action RAT, Amadey, AppleSeed, AuTo Stealer, BADFLICK, BADNEWS, BLINDINGCAN, BRICKSTORM. Recommended mitigations include Data Loss Prevention. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Access, File Creation, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may search local system sources, such as file systems, configuration files, local databases, virtual machine files, or process memory, to find files of interest and sensitive data prior to Exfiltration.",
