    "embedding_text": "Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information (T1140) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may use [Obfuscated Files or Information](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1027) to hide artifacts of an intrusion from analysis. They may require separate mechanisms to decode or deobfuscate that information depending on how they intend to use it. Methods for doing that include built-in functionality of malware or by using utilities present on the system.\n\nOne such example is the use of [certutil](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0160) to decode a remote access tool portable e It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT19, APT28, APT38, APT39, Agrius, BRONZE BUTLER, BlackByte, Cinnamon Tempest and malware families such as ABK, ANELLDR, Action RAT, Agent Tesla, Amadey, Apostle, AppleJeus, AppleSeed. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Creation, Process Access, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may use [Obfuscated Files or Information](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1027) to hide artifacts of an intrusion from analysis.",
