    "embedding_text": "Archive via Library (T1560.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. An adversary may compress or encrypt data that is collected prior to exfiltration using 3rd party libraries. Many libraries exist that can archive data, including [Python](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/006) rarfile (Citation: PyPI RAR), libzip (Citation: libzip), and zlib (Citation: Zlib Github). Most libraries include functionality to encrypt and/or compress data.\n\nSome archival libraries are preinstalled on systems, such as bzip2 on macOS and Linux, and zip on Windows. Note that th It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by Lazarus Group, Threat Group-3390 and malware families such as BADFLICK, BBSRAT, Cardinal RAT, Denis, Epic, FoggyWeb, FunnyDream, InvisiMole. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Creation, Module Load, Process Creation.",
