    "embedding_text": "Masquerading (T1036) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may attempt to manipulate features of their artifacts to make them appear legitimate or benign to users and/or security tools. Masquerading occurs when the name or location of an object, legitimate or malicious, is manipulated or abused for the sake of evading defenses and observation. This may include manipulating file metadata, tricking users into misidentifying the file type, and giving legitimate task or service names.\n\nRenaming abusable system utilities to evade security monitor It affects Containers, ESXi, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, APT32, Agrius, Aoqin Dragon, BRONZE BUTLER, Contagious Interview, Ember Bear, FIN13 and malware families such as AppleSeed, BeaverTail, Bisonal, BoomBox, Dacls, DarkGate, DarkTortilla, DarkWatchman. Recommended mitigations include Audit, User Account Management, User Training, Code Signing, Behavior Prevention on Endpoint. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Metadata, File Modification, Image Metadata, Process Creation.",
