    "embedding_text": "Unsecured Credentials (T1552) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Credential Access tactic. Adversaries may search compromised systems to find and obtain insecurely stored credentials. These credentials can be stored and/or misplaced in many locations on a system, including plaintext files (e.g. [Shell History](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/003)), operating system or application-specific repositories (e.g. [Credentials in Registry](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/002)),  or other specialized files/artifacts (e.g. [Private Keys](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/ It affects Windows, SaaS, IaaS, Linux, macOS, Containers, Network Devices, Office Suite, Identity Provider platforms and has been observed used by Volt Typhoon and malware families such as Astaroth, DarkGate. Recommended mitigations include Encrypt Sensitive Information, Update Software, User Training, Active Directory Configuration, Password Policies. Detection relies on Application Log Content, Cloud Service Metadata, Command Execution, File Access, File Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may search compromised systems to find and obtain insecurely stored credentials.",
