    "embedding_text": "Content Injection (T1659) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Initial Access, Command and Control tactic. Adversaries may gain access and continuously communicate with victims by injecting malicious content into systems through online network traffic. Rather than luring victims to malicious payloads hosted on a compromised website (i.e., [Drive-by Target](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1608/004) followed by [Drive-by Compromise](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1189)), adversaries may initially access victims through compromised data-transfer channels where they can manipulate traffic and/ It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by MoustachedBouncer and malware families such as Disco. Recommended mitigations include Restrict Web-Based Content, Encrypt Sensitive Information. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Creation, Network Traffic Content, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may gain access and continuously communicate with victims by injecting malicious content into systems through online network traffic.",
