    "embedding_text": "Process Injection (T1055) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth, Privilege Escalation tactic. Adversaries may inject code into processes in order to evade process-based defenses as well as possibly elevate privileges. Process injection is a method of executing arbitrary code in the address space of a separate live process. Running code in the context of another process may allow access to the process's memory, system/network resources, and possibly elevated privileges. Execution via process injection may also evade detection from security products since the execution is masked under a le It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT32, APT37, APT38, APT41, APT5, BlackByte, Cobalt Group, Gamaredon Group and malware families such as ABK, ANDROMEDA, Agent Tesla, Attor, AuditCred, Avenger, BADHATCH, BBK. Recommended mitigations include Privileged Account Management, Behavior Prevention on Endpoint. Detection relies on File Access, Module Load, OS API Execution, Process Access, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may inject code into processes in order to evade process-based defenses as well as possibly elevate privileges.",
