    "embedding_text": "Mutual Exclusion (T1480.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may constrain execution or actions based on the presence of a mutex associated with malware. A mutex is a locking mechanism used to synchronize access to a resource. Only one thread or process can acquire a mutex at a given time.(Citation: Microsoft Mutexes)\n\nWhile local mutexes only exist within a given process, allowing multiple threads to synchronize access to a resource, system mutexes can be used to synchronize the activities of multiple processes.(Citation: Microsoft Mutexes) B It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT38, Kimsuky and malware families such as BPFDoor, Black Basta, CLAIMLOADER, Embargo, Gazer, GrimAgent, HiddenFace, LockBit 3.0. Recommended mitigations include Do Not Mitigate. Detection relies on File Access, File Creation, OS API Execution, Process Creation, Process Termination.",
