    "embedding_text": "Time Based Checks (T1497.003) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth, Discovery tactic. Adversaries may employ various time-based methods to detect virtualization and analysis environments, particularly those that attempt to manipulate time mechanisms to simulate longer elapses of time. This may include enumerating time-based properties, such as uptime or the system clock. \n\nAdversaries may use calls like `GetTickCount` and `GetSystemTimeAsFileTime` to discover if they are operating within a virtual machine or sandbox, or may be able to identify a sandbox accelerating time by sampl It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors and malware families such as AppleJeus, BADFLICK, Bazar, BendyBear, Bisonal, Bumblebee, Clambling, Clop. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on File Metadata, Module Load, OS API Execution, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may employ various time-based methods to detect virtualization and analysis environments, particularly those that attempt to manipulate time mechanisms to simulate longer elapses of time.",
