    "embedding_text": "Scheduled Transfer (T1029) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Exfiltration tactic. Adversaries may schedule data exfiltration to be performed only at certain times of day or at certain intervals. This could be done to blend traffic patterns with normal activity or availability.\n\nWhen scheduled exfiltration is used, other exfiltration techniques likely apply as well to transfer the information out of the network, such as [Exfiltration Over C2 Channel](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1041) or [Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1048 It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by Higaisa and malware families such as ADVSTORESHELL, Chrommme, Cobalt Strike, ComRAT, Dipsind, Flagpro, Kazuar, LightNeuron. Recommended mitigations include Network Intrusion Prevention. Detection relies on Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Flow, Process Creation, Scheduled Job Metadata.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may schedule data exfiltration to be performed only at certain times of day or at certain intervals.",
