    "embedding_text": "SMB/Windows Admin Shares (T1021.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Lateral Movement tactic. Adversaries may use [Valid Accounts](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1078) to interact with a remote network share using Server Message Block (SMB). The adversary may then perform actions as the logged-on user.\n\nSMB is a file, printer, and serial port sharing protocol for Windows machines on the same network or domain. Adversaries may use SMB to interact with file shares, allowing them to move laterally throughout a network. Linux and macOS implementations of SMB typically use Samba.\n\nWindo It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, APT3, APT32, APT39, APT41, Aquatic Panda, BlackByte, Blue Mockingbird and malware families such as Anchor, BlackByte Ransomware, BlackEnergy, Cobalt Strike, Conficker, Conti, Diavol, Duqu. Recommended mitigations include Privileged Account Management, Limit Access to Resource Over Network, Filter Network Traffic, Password Policies. Detection relies on Logon Session Creation, Network Connection Creation, Process Creation.",
