    "beginner_explanation": "Network Device Configuration Dump is a technique attackers use during the Collection stage of an intrusion. In simple terms: Adversaries may access network configuration files to collect sensitive data about the device and the network.",
    "analyst_explanation": "Adversaries may access network configuration files to collect sensitive data about the device and the network. The network configuration is a file containing parameters that determine the operation of the device. The device typically stores an in-memory copy of the configuration while operating, and a separate configuration on non-volatile storage to load after device reset. Adversaries can inspect the configuration files to reveal information about the target network and its layout, the network device and its software, or identifying legitimate accounts and credentials for later use.\n\nAdversa",
