    "embedding_text": "Archive Collected Data (T1560) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. An adversary may compress and/or encrypt data that is collected prior to exfiltration. Compressing the data can help to obfuscate the collected data and minimize the amount of data sent over the network.(Citation: DOJ GRU Indictment Jul 2018) Encryption can be used to hide information that is being exfiltrated from detection or make exfiltration less conspicuous upon inspection by a defender.\n\nBoth compression and encryption are done prior to exfiltration, and can be performed using a utility, 3 It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, APT32, Axiom, BlackByte, Dragonfly, Ember Bear, FIN6, Ke3chang and malware families such as ADVSTORESHELL, Agent Tesla, AppleSeed, Aria-body, BLUELIGHT, Backdoor.Oldrea, Bumblebee, Cadelspy. Recommended mitigations include Audit. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Creation, Module Load, Process Creation.",
