    "embedding_text": "Modify Registry (T1112) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Defense Impairment, Persistence tactic. Adversaries may interact with the Windows Registry as part of a variety of other techniques to aid in defense evasion, persistence, and execution.\n\nAccess to specific areas of the Registry depends on account permissions, with some keys requiring administrator-level access. The built-in Windows command-line utility [Reg](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0075) may be used for local or remote Registry modification.(Citation: Microsoft Reg) Other tools, such as remote access tools, may also contai It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT19, APT32, APT38, APT41, APT42, Aquatic Panda, BlackByte, Blue Mockingbird and malware families such as ADVSTORESHELL, Agent Tesla, Amadey, Attor, Avaddon, BACKSPACE, BADCALL, BOOKWORM. Recommended mitigations include Restrict Registry Permissions. Detection relies on Process Creation, Windows Registry Key Modification.",
