    "embedding_text": "Launch Daemon (T1543.004) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Persistence, Privilege Escalation tactic. Adversaries may create or modify Launch Daemons to execute malicious payloads as part of persistence. Launch Daemons are plist files used to interact with Launchd, the service management framework used by macOS. Launch Daemons require elevated privileges to install, are executed for every user on a system prior to login, and run in the background without the need for user interaction. During the macOS initialization startup, the launchd process loads the parameters for launch-on-demand system-le It affects macOS platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors and malware families such as AppleJeus, Bundlore, COATHANGER, Dacls, Green Lambert, LoudMiner, OSX_OCEANLOTUS.D, REPTILE. Recommended mitigations include User Account Management, Audit. Detection relies on File Creation, File Modification, Process Creation, Service Creation.",
