    "embedding_text": "Binary Padding (T1027.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may use binary padding to add junk data and change the on-disk representation of malware. This can be done without affecting the functionality or behavior of a binary, but can increase the size of the binary beyond what some security tools are capable of handling due to file size limitations. \n\nBinary padding effectively changes the checksum of the file and can also be used to avoid hash-based blocklists and static anti-virus signatures.(Citation: ESET OceanLotus) The padding used is It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT29, Akira, BRONZE BUTLER, Higaisa, Kimsuky, Leviathan, Moafee, Patchwork and malware families such as Bisonal, Black Basta, CHIMNEYSWEEP, Caminho, Comnie, CostaBricks, Emissary, Emotet. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on File Access, File Creation, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may use binary padding to add junk data and change the on-disk representation of malware.",
