    "embedding_text": "Private Keys (T1552.004) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Credential Access tactic. Adversaries may search for private key certificate files on compromised systems for insecurely stored credentials. Private cryptographic keys and certificates are used for authentication, encryption/decryption, and digital signatures.(Citation: Wikipedia Public Key Crypto) Common key and certificate file extensions include: .key, .pgp, .gpg, .ppk., .p12, .pem, .pfx, .cer, .p7b, .asc. \n\nAdversaries may also look in common key directories, such as <code>~/.ssh</code> for SSH keys on * nix-based sy It affects Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows platforms and has been observed used by Kimsuky, Rocke, Scattered Spider, Storm-0501, TeamTNT, Volt Typhoon and malware families such as Ebury, FoggyWeb, Hildegard, Kinsing, Machete, Mafalda, Troll Stealer, jRAT. Recommended mitigations include Password Policies, Restrict File and Directory Permissions, Audit, Encrypt Sensitive Information. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Access, File Creation, Network Share Access, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may search for private key certificate files on compromised systems for insecurely stored credentials.",
