    "embedding_text": "Communication Through Removable Media (T1092) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Command and Control tactic. Adversaries can perform command and control between compromised hosts on potentially disconnected networks using removable media to transfer commands from system to system.(Citation: ESET Sednit USBStealer 2014) Both systems would need to be compromised, with the likelihood that an Internet-connected system was compromised first and the second through lateral movement by [Replication Through Removable Media](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1091). Commands and files would be relayed from the It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28 and malware families such as CHOPSTICK, USBStealer. Recommended mitigations include Disable or Remove Feature or Program, Operating System Configuration. Detection relies on Drive Creation, File Creation, Process Creation.",
