    "embedding_text": "File and Directory Permissions Modification (T1222) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Defense Impairment tactic. Adversaries may modify file or directory permissions/attributes to evade access control lists (ACLs) and access protected files.(Citation: Hybrid Analysis Icacls1 June 2018)(Citation: Hybrid Analysis Icacls2 May 2018) File and directory permissions are commonly managed by ACLs configured by the file or directory owner, or users with the appropriate permissions. File and directory ACL implementations vary by platform, but generally explicitly designate which users or groups can perform which acti It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors and malware families such as Qilin. Recommended mitigations include Restrict File and Directory Permissions, Privileged Account Management. Detection relies on Active Directory Object Modification, Command Execution, File Creation, File Metadata, Process Creation.",
