    "embedding_text": "System Network Configuration Discovery (T1016) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Discovery tactic. Adversaries may look for details about the network configuration and settings, such as IP and/or MAC addresses, of systems they access or through information discovery of remote systems. Several operating system administration utilities exist that can be used to gather this information. Examples include [Arp](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0099), [ipconfig](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0100)/[ifconfig](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0101), [nbtstat](https://attack.mitre.org/softwar It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT1, APT19, APT3, APT32, APT41, APT42, BlackByte, Chimera and malware families such as Action RAT, Agent Tesla, Agent.btz, Amadey, Anchor, AppleSeed, Aria-body, Astaroth. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Command Execution, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may look for details about the network configuration and settings, such as IP and/or MAC addresses, of systems they access or through information discovery of remote systems.",
