    "embedding_text": "Account Discovery (T1087) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Discovery tactic. Adversaries may attempt to get a listing of valid accounts, usernames, or email addresses on a system or within a compromised environment. This information can help adversaries determine which accounts exist, which can aid in follow-on behavior such as brute-forcing, spear-phishing attacks, or account takeovers (e.g., [Valid Accounts](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1078)).\n\nAdversaries may use several methods to enumerate accounts, including abuse of existing tools, built-in commands, and  It affects ESXi, IaaS, Identity Provider, Linux, macOS, Office Suite, SaaS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by Aquatic Panda, FIN13, Scattered Spider and malware families such as Havoc, TONESHELL, Woody RAT, XCSSET. Recommended mitigations include Operating System Configuration, User Account Management. Detection relies on Cloud Service Enumeration, Command Execution, File Access, Group Enumeration, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may attempt to get a listing of valid accounts, usernames, or email addresses on a system or within a compromised environment.",
