    "embedding_text": "Proxy (T1090) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Command and Control tactic. Adversaries may use a connection proxy to direct network traffic between systems or act as an intermediary for network communications to a command and control server to avoid direct connections to their infrastructure. Many tools exist that enable traffic redirection through proxies or port redirection, including [HTRAN](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0040), ZXProxy, and ZXPortMap. (Citation: Trend Micro APT Attack Tools) Adversaries use these types of proxies to manage command and control c It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT41, Blue Mockingbird, Cinnamon Tempest, Contagious Interview, CopyKittens, Earth Lusca, Fox Kitten, Gamaredon Group and malware families such as Aria-body, AuditCred, BADCALL, BADHATCH, Bisonal, Cardinal RAT, Dridex, FunnyDream. Recommended mitigations include Filter Network Traffic, Network Intrusion Prevention, SSL/TLS Inspection. Detection relies on Command Execution, Firewall Rule Modification, Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Flow, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may use a connection proxy to direct network traffic between systems or act as an intermediary for network communications to a command and control server to avoid direct connections to their infrastructure.",
