    "embedding_text": "Indicator Removal (T1070) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may selectively delete or modify artifacts generated to reduce indications of their presence and blend in with legitimate activity. Rather than broadly removing evidence, adversaries may target specific artifacts that appear anomalous or are likely to draw scrutiny, while leaving sufficient data intact to maintain the appearance of normal system behavior.\n\nArtifacts such as command histories, log entries, or file metadata may be altered in ways that align with expected user or system It affects Containers, ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Office Suite, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT42, APT5, Lazarus Group, Mustang Panda and malware families such as BPFDoor, Bankshot, BlackEnergy, DUSTTRAP, DarkWatchman, EVILNUM, Flagpro, FunnyDream. Recommended mitigations include Encrypt Sensitive Information, Remote Data Storage, Restrict File and Directory Permissions. Detection relies on Application Log Content, File Deletion, File Metadata, File Modification, Scheduled Job Modification.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may selectively delete or modify artifacts generated to reduce indications of their presence and blend in with legitimate activity.",
