    "embedding_text": "Exfiltration Over Symmetric Encrypted Non-C2 Protocol (T1048.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Exfiltration tactic. Adversaries may steal data by exfiltrating it over a symmetrically encrypted network protocol other than that of the existing command and control channel. The data may also be sent to an alternate network location from the main command and control server. \n\nSymmetric encryption algorithms are those that use shared or the same keys/secrets on each end of the channel. This requires an exchange or pre-arranged agreement/possession of the value used to encrypt and decrypt data. \n\nNetwork protocols t It affects Linux, macOS, Windows, ESXi platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors . Recommended mitigations include Filter Network Traffic, Network Intrusion Prevention, Network Segmentation. Detection relies on Command Execution, Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Content, Network Traffic Flow, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may steal data by exfiltrating it over a symmetrically encrypted network protocol other than that of the existing command and control channel.",
