    "embedding_text": "Pass the Ticket (T1550.003) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Lateral Movement tactic. Adversaries may “pass the ticket” using stolen Kerberos tickets to move laterally within an environment, bypassing normal system access controls. Pass the ticket (PtT) is a method of authenticating to a system using Kerberos tickets without having access to an account's password. Kerberos authentication can be used as the first step to lateral movement to a remote system.\n\nWhen preforming PtT, valid Kerberos tickets for [Valid Accounts](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1078) are captured by  It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT29, APT32, BRONZE BUTLER and malware families such as SeaDuke. Recommended mitigations include Privileged Account Management, Password Policies, User Account Management, Active Directory Configuration. Detection relies on Active Directory Credential Request, Logon Session Creation, Module Load, Process Access, User Account Authentication.",
