    "embedding_text": "File and Directory Discovery (T1083) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Discovery tactic. Adversaries may enumerate files and directories or may search in specific locations of a host or network share for certain information within a file system. Adversaries may use the information from [File and Directory Discovery](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1083) during automated discovery to shape follow-on behaviors, including whether or not the adversary fully infects the target and/or attempts specific actions.\n\nMany command shell utilities can be used to obtain this information. Exa It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT18, APT28, APT3, APT32, APT38, APT39, APT41, APT5 and malware families such as 3PARA RAT, 4H RAT, ADVSTORESHELL, ANELLDR, AcidPour, AcidRain, Action RAT, Akira. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Access, File Creation, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may enumerate files and directories or may search in specific locations of a host or network share for certain information within a file system.",
