    "embedding_text": "Masquerade Task or Service (T1036.004) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may attempt to manipulate the name of a task or service to make it appear legitimate or benign. Tasks/services executed by the Task Scheduler or systemd will typically be given a name and/or description.(Citation: TechNet Schtasks)(Citation: Systemd Service Units) Windows services will have a service name as well as a display name. Many benign tasks and services exist that have commonly associated names. Adversaries may give tasks or services names that are similar or identical to th It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT-C-36, APT32, APT41, Aquatic Panda, BITTER, BackdoorDiplomacy, Carbanak, FIN13 and malware families such as Attor, BOOKWORM, Bazar, Black Basta, Catchamas, ComRAT, Crutch, DCSrv. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Process Creation, Scheduled Job Creation, Scheduled Job Metadata, Scheduled Job Modification, Service Creation.",
