    "embedding_text": "Data Staged (T1074) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. Adversaries may stage collected data in a central location or directory prior to Exfiltration. Data may be kept in separate files or combined into one file through techniques such as [Archive Collected Data](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1560). Interactive command shells may be used, and common functionality within [cmd](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0106) and bash may be used to copy data into a staging location.(Citation: PWC Cloud Hopper April 2017)\n\nIn cloud environments, adversa It affects ESXi, IaaS, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by INC Ransom, Scattered Spider, VOID MANTICORE, Volt Typhoon, Wizard Spider and malware families such as Kevin, Kobalos, QUIETCANARY, Shark. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Cloud Storage Access, Command Execution, File Access, File Creation, Process Creation.",
