    "embedding_text": "Log Enumeration (T1654) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Discovery tactic. Adversaries may enumerate system and service logs to find useful data. These logs may highlight various types of valuable insights for an adversary, such as user authentication records ([Account Discovery](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1087)), security or vulnerable software ([Software Discovery](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1518)), or hosts within a compromised network ([Remote System Discovery](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1018)).\n\nHost binaries may be leveraged to colle It affects ESXi, IaaS, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT5, Aquatic Panda, Ember Bear, Mustang Panda, Volt Typhoon and malware families such as Akira _v2, BeaverTail, DUSTTRAP, Megazord. Recommended mitigations include User Account Management. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Access, Process Creation.",
