    "embedding_text": "Internal Defacement (T1491.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Impact tactic. An adversary may deface systems internal to an organization in an attempt to intimidate or mislead users, thus discrediting the integrity of the systems. This may take the form of modifications to internal websites or server login messages, or directly to user systems with the replacement of the desktop wallpaper.(Citation: Novetta Blockbuster)(Citation: Varonis) Disturbing or offensive images may be used as a part of [Internal Defacement](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1491/001) in order  It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by BlackByte, Gamaredon Group, Lazarus Group and malware families such as Black Basta, BlackCat, Diavol, INC Ransomware, Meteor, Qilin, ROADSWEEP, RansomHub. Recommended mitigations include Data Backup. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Access, File Creation, File Modification, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "An adversary may deface systems internal to an organization in an attempt to intimidate or mislead users, thus discrediting the integrity of the systems.",
