    "embedding_text": "Exfiltration Over Asymmetric Encrypted Non-C2 Protocol (T1048.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Exfiltration tactic. Adversaries may steal data by exfiltrating it over an asymmetrically encrypted network protocol other than that of the existing command and control channel. The data may also be sent to an alternate network location from the main command and control server. \n\nAsymmetric encryption algorithms are those that use different keys on each end of the channel. Also known as public-key cryptography, this requires pairs of cryptographic keys that can encrypt/decrypt data from the corresponding key. Each e It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, CURIUM, MirrorFace, Storm-1811 and malware families such as BRUSHFIRE, IcedID. Recommended mitigations include Network Intrusion Prevention, Network Segmentation, Filter Network Traffic, Data Loss Prevention. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Access, Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Content, Network Traffic Flow.",
