    "embedding_text": "Process Discovery (T1057) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Discovery tactic. Adversaries may attempt to get information about running processes on a system. Information obtained could be used to gain an understanding of common software/applications running on systems within the network. Administrator or otherwise elevated access may provide better process details. Adversaries may use the information from [Process Discovery](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1057) during automated discovery to shape follow-on behaviors, including whether or not the adversary fully infe It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT1, APT28, APT3, APT37, APT38, APT5, Andariel, Chimera and malware families such as 4H RAT, ADVSTORESHELL, Agent Tesla, Akira, Apostle, AppleSeed, Aria-body, AshTag. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Access, Process Access, Process Creation, Process Metadata.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may attempt to get information about running processes on a system.",
