    "embedding_text": "Network Provider DLL (T1556.008) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Defense Impairment, Persistence, Credential Access tactic. Adversaries may register malicious network provider dynamic link libraries (DLLs) to capture cleartext user credentials during the authentication process. Network provider DLLs allow Windows to interface with specific network protocols and can also support add-on credential management functions.(Citation: Network Provider API) During the logon process, Winlogon (the interactive logon module) sends credentials to the local `mpnotify.exe` process via RPC. The `mpnotify.exe` process then shares the It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors . Recommended mitigations include Restrict Registry Permissions, Audit, Operating System Configuration. Detection relies on File Creation, Module Load, Process Access, Windows Registry Key Modification.",
