    "embedding_text": "Exfiltration Over C2 Channel (T1041) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Exfiltration tactic. Adversaries may steal data by exfiltrating it over an existing command and control channel. Stolen data is encoded into the normal communications channel using the same protocol as command and control communications. It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT3, APT32, APT39, Agrius, BlackByte, CURIUM, Chimera, Confucius and malware families such as ADVSTORESHELL, Amadey, AppleJeus, AppleSeed, AshTag, Astaroth, Attor, AuTo Stealer. Recommended mitigations include Network Intrusion Prevention, Data Loss Prevention. Detection relies on File Access, Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Content, Network Traffic Flow, Process Creation.",
