    "embedding_text": "File Transfer Protocols (T1071.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Command and Control tactic. Adversaries may communicate using application layer protocols associated with transferring files to avoid detection/network filtering by blending in with existing traffic. Commands to the remote system, and often the results of those commands, will be embedded within the protocol traffic between the client and server. \n\nProtocols such as SMB(Citation: US-CERT TA18-074A), FTP(Citation: ESET Machete July 2019), FTPS, and TFTP that transfer files may be very common in environments.  Packets produce It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT41, Dragonfly, Kimsuky, MirrorFace, SilverTerrier and malware families such as Attor, BADHATCH, Cobalt Strike, Disco, Havoc, JPIN, Kazuar, Machete. Recommended mitigations include Filter Network Traffic, Network Intrusion Prevention. Detection relies on Command Execution, Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Content, Network Traffic Flow, Process Creation.",
