    "embedding_text": "Delay Execution (T1678) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may employ various time-based methods to evade detection and analysis. These techniques often exploit system clocks, delays, or timing mechanisms to obscure malicious activity, blend in with benign activity, and avoid scrutiny. Adversaries can perform this behavior within virtualization/sandbox environments or natively on host systems. \n\nAdversaries may utilize programmatic `sleep` commands or native system scheduling functionality, for example [Scheduled Task/Job](https://attack.mit It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by Kimsuky, Mustang Panda and malware families such as AshTag, BRICKSTORM, DynoWiper, Fooder, GlassWorm, HIUPAN, MuddyViper, PHASEJAM. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Module Load, Process Creation, Script Execution.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may employ various time-based methods to evade detection and analysis.",
