    "embedding_text": "Network Device Firewall (T1686.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Defense Impairment tactic. Adversaries may disable network device-based firewall mechanisms entirely or add, delete, or modify particular rules in order to bypass controls limiting network usage.  \n\nAdversaries may obtain access to devices such as routers, switches, or other perimeter/network devices and change access control lists (ACLs), security zones, or policy rules to permit otherwise blocked traffic. For example, adversaries may add new network firewall rules to allow access to all internal network subnets without  It affects Network Devices platforms and has been observed used by APT38 and malware families such as Cyclops Blink, Grandoreiro. Recommended mitigations include Update Software, Audit, User Account Management. Detection relies on Command Execution, Firewall Rule Modification, Logon Session Creation, Network Connection Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may disable network device-based firewall mechanisms entirely or add, delete, or modify particular rules in order to bypass controls limiting network usage.",
