    "embedding_text": "Tool (T1588.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Resource Development tactic. Adversaries may buy, steal, or download software tools that can be used during targeting. Tools can be open or closed source, free or commercial. A tool can be used for malicious purposes by an adversary, but (unlike malware) were not intended to be used for those purposes (ex: [PsExec](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0029)). \n\nAdversaries may obtain tools to support their operations, including to support execution of post-compromise behaviors. Tools may also be leveraged for testing – for ex It affects PRE platforms and has been observed used by APT-C-36, APT1, APT19, APT28, APT29, APT32, APT33, APT38 and malware families such as Lizar. Recommended mitigations include Pre-compromise. Detection relies on Malware Metadata.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may buy, steal, or download software tools that can be used during targeting.",
