    "embedding_text": "Exfiltration over USB (T1052.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Exfiltration tactic. Adversaries may attempt to exfiltrate data over a USB connected physical device. In certain circumstances, such as an air-gapped network compromise, exfiltration could occur via a USB device introduced by a user. The USB device could be used as the final exfiltration point or to hop between otherwise disconnected systems. It affects Linux, Windows, macOS platforms and has been observed used by Mustang Panda, Tropic Trooper and malware families such as Agent.btz, Machete, Remsec, SPACESHIP, USBStealer. Recommended mitigations include Disable or Remove Feature or Program, Limit Hardware Installation, Data Loss Prevention. Detection relies on Drive Creation, File Access, File Creation, Process Creation.",
