    "embedding_text": "Network Share Connection Removal (T1070.005) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may remove share connections that are no longer useful in order to clean up traces of their operation. Windows shared drive and [SMB/Windows Admin Shares](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1021/002) connections can be removed when no longer needed. [Net](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0039) is an example utility that can be used to remove network share connections with the <code>net use \\\\system\\share /delete</code> command. (Citation: Technet Net Use) It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by Threat Group-3390 and malware families such as DUSTTRAP, InvisiMole, RobbinHood. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Command Execution, Logon Session Creation, Network Traffic Content, Process Creation.",
