    "beginner_explanation": "Brute Force is a technique attackers use during the Credential Access stage of an intrusion. In simple terms: Adversaries may use brute force techniques to gain access to accounts when passwords are unknown or when password hashes are obtained.(Citation: TrendMicro Pawn Storm Dec 2020) Without knowledge of the password for an account or set of accounts, an adversary may systematically guess the password using a repetitive or iterative mechanism.(Citation: Dragos Crashoverride 2018) Brute forcing passwords can take place via interaction with a service that will check the validity of those credentials or offline against previously acquired credential data, such as password hashes.",
    "analyst_explanation": "Adversaries may use brute force techniques to gain access to accounts when passwords are unknown or when password hashes are obtained.(Citation: TrendMicro Pawn Storm Dec 2020) Without knowledge of the password for an account or set of accounts, an adversary may systematically guess the password using a repetitive or iterative mechanism.(Citation: Dragos Crashoverride 2018) Brute forcing passwords can take place via interaction with a service that will check the validity of those credentials or offline against previously acquired credential data, such as password hashes.\n\nBrute forcing credent",
    "executive_summary": "Brute Force (T1110) is a high-severity technique observed in real-world use by 20 known threat actor(s)/malware families, primarily impacting Containers, ESXi, IaaS, Identity Provider, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Office Suite, SaaS, Windows.",
    "attacker_view": "An attacker leverages Brute Force to advance the 'Credential Access' objective, typically requiring access to a Containers, ESXi, IaaS, Identity Provider, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Office Suite, SaaS, Windows system.",
    "defender_view": "Defenders should monitor User Account Authentication and apply mitigations such as User Account Management, Account Use Policies, Multi-factor Authentication to reduce exposure to Brute Force.",
    "detection_story": "This technique can be surfaced by correlating Brute Force Authentication Failures with Multi-Platform Log Correlation.",
