    "embedding_text": "Data Manipulation (T1565) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Impact tactic. Adversaries may insert, delete, or manipulate data in order to influence external outcomes or hide activity, thus threatening the integrity of the data.(Citation: Sygnia Elephant Beetle Jan 2022) By manipulating data, adversaries may attempt to affect a business process, organizational understanding, or decision making.\n\nThe type of modification and the impact it will have depends on the target application and process as well as the goals and objectives of the adversary. For complex systems, an  It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by FIN13 and malware families such as PHASEJAM. Recommended mitigations include Encrypt Sensitive Information, Remote Data Storage, Network Segmentation, Restrict File and Directory Permissions. Detection relies on File Access, File Creation, File Metadata, File Modification, Network Traffic Content.",
