    "embedding_text": "Data from Network Shared Drive (T1039) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. Adversaries may search network shares on computers they have compromised to find files of interest. Sensitive data can be collected from remote systems via shared network drives (host shared directory, network file server, etc.) that are accessible from the current system prior to Exfiltration. Interactive command shells may be in use, and common functionality within [cmd](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0106) may be used to gather information. It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT28, BRONZE BUTLER, Chimera, Fox Kitten, Gamaredon Group, RedCurl, Sowbug, menuPass and malware families such as BADNEWS, CosmicDuke, Egregor, Ramsay. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Drive Access, File Access, File Creation, Network Share Access.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may search network shares on computers they have compromised to find files of interest.",
