    "embedding_text": "Modify System Image (T1601) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Defense Impairment tactic. Adversaries may make changes to the operating system of embedded network devices to weaken defenses and provide new capabilities for themselves.  On such devices, the operating systems are typically monolithic and most of the device functionality and capabilities are contained within a single file.\n\nTo change the operating system, the adversary typically only needs to affect this one file, replacing or modifying it.  This can either be done live in memory during system runtime for immediate effe It affects Network Devices platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors and malware families such as DRYHOOK. Recommended mitigations include Multi-factor Authentication, Password Policies, Credential Access Protection, Code Signing, Boot Integrity. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Modification.",
