    "embedding_text": "Indicator Removal from Tools (T1027.005) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may remove indicators from tools if they believe their malicious tool was detected, quarantined, or otherwise curtailed. They can modify the tool by removing the indicator and using the updated version that is no longer detected by the target's defensive systems or subsequent targets that may use similar systems.\n\nA good example of this is when malware is detected with a file signature and quarantined by anti-virus software. An adversary who can determine that the malware was quarant It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT3, Deep Panda, GALLIUM, OilRig, Patchwork, Turla, UNC3886 and malware families such as Cobalt Strike, Daserf, GravityRAT, InvisiMole, Penquin, QakBot, SUNBURST, Waterbear. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Application Log Content, File Creation, File Metadata, Process Creation, Process Modification.",
