    "embedding_text": "Non-Standard Port (T1571) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Command and Control tactic. Adversaries may communicate using a protocol and port pairing that are typically not associated. For example, HTTPS over port 8088(Citation: Symantec Elfin Mar 2019) or port 587(Citation: Fortinet Agent Tesla April 2018) as opposed to the traditional port 443. Adversaries may make changes to the standard port used by a protocol to bypass filtering or muddle analysis/parsing of network data.\n\nAdversaries may also make changes to victim systems to abuse non-standard ports. For example, Registry ke It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT-C-36, APT32, APT33, Contagious Interview, DarkVishnya, Ember Bear, FIN7, Gamaredon Group and malware families such as BADCALL, Bankshot, BeaverTail, BendyBear, Cyclops Blink, Derusbi, Emotet, GlassWorm. Recommended mitigations include Network Segmentation, Network Intrusion Prevention. Detection relies on Application Log Content, Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Content, Network Traffic Flow, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may communicate using a protocol and port pairing that are typically not associated.",
