    "embedding_text": "Process Hollowing (T1055.012) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth, Privilege Escalation tactic. Adversaries may inject malicious code into suspended and hollowed processes in order to evade process-based defenses. Process hollowing is a method of executing arbitrary code in the address space of a separate live process.  \n\nProcess hollowing is commonly performed by creating a process in a suspended state then unmapping/hollowing its memory, which can then be replaced with malicious code. A victim process can be created with native Windows API calls such as <code>CreateProcess</code>, which  It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT-C-36, BlackByte, Gorgon Group, Kimsuky, Patchwork, TA2541, Threat Group-3390, menuPass and malware families such as Agent Tesla, Astaroth, Azorult, BADNEWS, BBSRAT, Bandook, Bazar, Caminho. Recommended mitigations include Behavior Prevention on Endpoint. Detection relies on OS API Execution, Process Access, Process Creation, Process Modification.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may inject malicious code into suspended and hollowed processes in order to evade process-based defenses.",
