    "embedding_text": "Remote Email Collection (T1114.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection tactic. Adversaries may target an Exchange server, Office 365, or Google Workspace to collect sensitive information. Adversaries may leverage a user's credentials and interact directly with the Exchange server to acquire information from within a network. Adversaries may also access externally facing Exchange services, Office 365, or Google Workspace to access email using credentials or access tokens. Tools such as [MailSniper](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0413) can be used to automate searches fo It affects Office Suite, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT1, APT28, APT29, Chimera, Dragonfly, FIN4, HAFNIUM, Ke3chang and malware families such as LightNeuron, SeaDuke, Valak. Recommended mitigations include Out-of-Band Communications Channel, Encrypt Sensitive Information, Multi-factor Authentication. Detection relies on Application Log Content, Command Execution, Logon Session Creation, Network Connection Creation.",
