    "embedding_text": "Polymorphic Code (T1027.014) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may utilize polymorphic code (also known as metamorphic or mutating code) to evade detection. Polymorphic code is a type of software capable of changing its runtime footprint during code execution.(Citation: polymorphic-blackberry) With each execution of the software, the code is mutated into a different version of itself that achieves the same purpose or objective as the original. This functionality enables the malware to evade traditional signature-based defenses, such as antivirus It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors and malware families such as BendyBear. Recommended mitigations include Behavior Prevention on Endpoint, Antivirus/Antimalware. Detection relies on File Creation, File Modification, Module Load, Process Access, Process Creation.",
