    "embedding_text": "SID-History Injection (T1134.005) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth, Privilege Escalation tactic. Adversaries may use SID-History Injection to escalate privileges and bypass access controls. The Windows security identifier (SID) is a unique value that identifies a user or group account. SIDs are used by Windows security in both security descriptors and access tokens. (Citation: Microsoft SID) An account can hold additional SIDs in the SID-History Active Directory attribute (Citation: Microsoft SID-History Attribute), allowing inter-operable account migration between domains (e.g., all values It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors . Recommended mitigations include Active Directory Configuration. Detection relies on Active Directory Object Modification, OS API Execution, User Account Metadata.",
