    "embedding_text": "Input Capture (T1056) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Collection, Credential Access tactic. Adversaries may use methods of capturing user input to obtain credentials or collect information. During normal system usage, users often provide credentials to various different locations, such as login pages/portals or system dialog boxes. Input capture mechanisms may be transparent to the user (e.g. [Credential API Hooking](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1056/004)) or rely on deceiving the user into providing input into what they believe to be a genuine service (e.g. [Web Portal Capture It affects Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT39, APT42, Storm-1811 and malware families such as Chaes, FlawedAmmyy, InvisibleFerret, Kobalos, Mafalda, metaMain. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on File Access, File Modification, Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Content, OS API Execution.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may use methods of capturing user input to obtain credentials or collect information.",
