    "embedding_text": "Outlook Home Page (T1137.004) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Persistence tactic. Adversaries may abuse Microsoft Outlook's Home Page feature to obtain persistence on a compromised system. Outlook Home Page is a legacy feature used to customize the presentation of Outlook folders. This feature allows for an internal or external URL to be loaded and presented whenever a folder is opened. A malicious HTML page can be crafted that will execute code when loaded by Outlook Home Page.(Citation: SensePost Outlook Home Page)\n\nOnce malicious home pages have been added to the user’s ma It affects Windows, Office Suite platforms and has been observed used by OilRig . Recommended mitigations include Update Software, Behavior Prevention on Endpoint. Detection relies on Application Log Content, Command Execution, Module Load, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may abuse Microsoft Outlook's Home Page feature to obtain persistence on a compromised system.",
