    "embedding_text": "Data Transfer Size Limits (T1030) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Exfiltration tactic. An adversary may exfiltrate data in fixed size chunks instead of whole files or limit packet sizes below certain thresholds. This approach may be used to avoid triggering network data transfer threshold alerts. It affects Linux, macOS, Windows, ESXi platforms and has been observed used by APT28, APT41, LuminousMoth, Play, Threat Group-3390 and malware families such as AppleSeed, Carbanak, Cobalt Strike, Helminth, Kessel, Kevin, LunarWeb, ObliqueRAT. Recommended mitigations include Network Intrusion Prevention. Detection relies on Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Flow.",
