    "embedding_text": "Network Logon Script (T1037.003) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Persistence, Privilege Escalation tactic. Adversaries may use network logon scripts automatically executed at logon initialization to establish persistence. Network logon scripts can be assigned using Active Directory or Group Policy Objects.(Citation: Petri Logon Script AD) These logon scripts run with the privileges of the user they are assigned to. Depending on the systems within the network, initializing one of these scripts could apply to more than one or potentially all systems.  \n \nAdversaries may use these scripts to maintain pe It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors . Recommended mitigations include Restrict File and Directory Permissions. Detection relies on Network Share Access, Process Creation, Script Execution.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may use network logon scripts automatically executed at logon initialization to establish persistence.",
