    "embedding_text": "Compile After Delivery (T1027.004) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may attempt to make payloads difficult to discover and analyze by delivering files to victims as uncompiled code. Text-based source code files may subvert analysis and scrutiny from protections targeting executables/binaries. These payloads will need to be compiled before execution; typically via native utilities such as ilasm.exe(Citation: ATTACK IQ), csc.exe, or GCC/MinGW.(Citation: ClearSky MuddyWater Nov 2018)\n\nSource code payloads may also be encrypted, encoded, and/or embedded  It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by Gamaredon Group, MuddyWater, Rocke, Sea Turtle and malware families such as Cardinal RAT, DarkWatchman, FoggyWeb, Samurai, njRAT. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on File Creation, Network Connection Creation, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may attempt to make payloads difficult to discover and analyze by delivering files to victims as uncompiled code.",
