    "embedding_text": "Python (T1059.006) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Execution tactic. Adversaries may abuse Python commands and scripts for execution. Python is a very popular scripting/programming language, with capabilities to perform many functions. Python can be executed interactively from the command-line (via the <code>python.exe</code> interpreter) or via scripts (.py) that can be written and distributed to different systems. Python code can also be compiled into binary executables.(Citation: Zscaler APT31 Covid-19 October 2020)\n\nPython comes with many built-in packages to It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT29, APT37, APT39, BRONZE BUTLER, Cinnamon Tempest, Contagious Interview, Dragonfly, Earth Lusca and malware families such as Bandook, Bundlore, Chaes, Cobalt Strike, CoinTicker, CookieMiner, DRYHOOK, DropBook. Recommended mitigations include Audit, Antivirus/Antimalware, Limit Software Installation, Execution Prevention. Detection relies on Command Execution, Network Traffic Content, Process Creation, Script Execution.",
