    "embedding_text": "Data Encoding (T1132) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Command and Control tactic. Adversaries may encode data to make the content of command and control traffic more difficult to detect. Command and control (C2) information can be encoded using a standard data encoding system. Use of data encoding may adhere to existing protocol specifications and includes use of ASCII, Unicode, Base64, MIME, or other binary-to-text and character encoding systems.(Citation: Wikipedia Binary-to-text Encoding) (Citation: Wikipedia Character Encoding) Some data encoding systems may also result i It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by Velvet Ant and malware families such as BADNEWS, H1N1, LAMEHUG, Linux Rabbit, Ursnif. Recommended mitigations include Network Intrusion Prevention. Detection relies on Command Execution, Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Content, Process Creation, User Account Authentication.",
