    "embedding_text": "Launch Agent (T1543.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Persistence, Privilege Escalation tactic. Adversaries may create or modify launch agents to repeatedly execute malicious payloads as part of persistence. When a user logs in, a per-user launchd process is started which loads the parameters for each launch-on-demand user agent from the property list (.plist) file found in <code>/System/Library/LaunchAgents</code>, <code>/Library/LaunchAgents</code>, and <code>~/Library/LaunchAgents</code>.(Citation: AppleDocs Launch Agent Daemons)(Citation: OSX Keydnap malware) (Citation: Antiquated Mac  It affects macOS platforms and has been observed used by Contagious Interview and malware families such as Bundlore, Calisto, CoinTicker, CookieMiner, CrossRAT, Cuckoo Stealer, Dacls, Dok. Recommended mitigations include Restrict File and Directory Permissions. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Creation, File Modification, Service Creation.",
