    "embedding_text": "Remote Desktop Software (T1219.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Command and Control tactic. An adversary may use legitimate desktop support software to establish an interactive command and control channel to target systems within networks. Desktop support software provides a graphical interface for remotely controlling another computer, transmitting the display output, keyboard input, and mouse control between devices using various protocols. Desktop support software, such as `VNC`, `Team Viewer`, `AnyDesk`, `ScreenConnect`, `LogMein`, `AmmyyAdmin`, and other remote monitoring and mana It affects Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by Contagious Interview, Evilnum, Kimsuky, MuddyWater, Mustang Panda, RTM, Scattered Spider, Storm-0501 and malware families such as Qilin. Recommended mitigations include Disable or Remove Feature or Program, Filter Network Traffic, Execution Prevention. Detection relies on File Creation, Firewall Rule Modification, Network Connection Creation, Process Creation.",
