    "embedding_text": "Server Software Component (T1505) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Persistence tactic. Adversaries may abuse legitimate extensible development features of servers to establish persistent access to systems. Enterprise server applications may include features that allow developers to write and install software or scripts to extend the functionality of the main application. Adversaries may install malicious components to extend and abuse server applications.(Citation: volexity_0day_sophos_FW) It affects Windows, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, ESXi platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors . Recommended mitigations include Code Signing, Audit, Restrict Registry Permissions, Disable or Remove Feature or Program, Boot Integrity. Detection relies on Application Log Content, Command Execution, Network Traffic Content, Network Traffic Flow, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may abuse legitimate extensible development features of servers to establish persistent access to systems.",
