    "embedding_text": "Drive-by Compromise (T1189) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Initial Access tactic. Adversaries may gain access to a system through a user visiting a website over the normal course of browsing. Multiple ways of delivering exploit code to a browser exist (i.e., [Drive-by Target](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1608/004)), including:\n\n* A legitimate website is compromised, allowing adversaries to inject malicious code\n* Script files served to a legitimate website from a publicly writeable cloud storage bucket are modified by an adversary\n* Malicious ads are paid for and serv It affects Identity Provider, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT19, APT28, APT32, APT37, APT38, Andariel, Axiom, BRONZE BUTLER and malware families such as Bad Rabbit, Bundlore, Grandoreiro, IcedID, KARAE, LoudMiner, POORAIM, REvil. Recommended mitigations include Exploit Protection, Update Software, Application Isolation and Sandboxing, Restrict Web-Based Content, User Training. Detection relies on Application Log Content, File Creation, Logon Session Creation, Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Content.",
