    "embedding_text": "Scanning IP Blocks (T1595.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Reconnaissance tactic. Adversaries may scan victim IP blocks to gather information that can be used during targeting. Public IP addresses may be allocated to organizations by block, or a range of sequential addresses.\n\nAdversaries may scan IP blocks in order to [Gather Victim Network Information](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1590), such as which IP addresses are actively in use as well as more detailed information about hosts assigned these addresses. Scans may range from simple pings (ICMP requests and respon It affects PRE platforms and has been observed used by Ember Bear, TeamTNT . Recommended mitigations include Pre-compromise. Detection relies on Network Traffic Content, Network Traffic Flow.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may scan victim IP blocks to gather information that can be used during targeting.",
