    "embedding_text": "Domain Properties (T1590.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Reconnaissance tactic. Adversaries may gather information about the victim's network domain(s) that can be used during targeting. Information about domains and their properties may include a variety of details, including what domain(s) the victim owns as well as administrative data (ex: name, registrar, etc.) and more directly actionable information such as contacts (email addresses and phone numbers), business addresses, and name servers.\n\nAdversaries may gather this information in various ways, such as direct collec It affects PRE platforms and has been observed used by Sandworm Team . Recommended mitigations include Pre-compromise. Detection relies on behavioral monitoring.",
