    "embedding_text": "Software Discovery (T1518) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Discovery tactic. Adversaries may attempt to get a listing of software and software versions that are installed on a system or in a cloud environment. Adversaries may use the information from [Software Discovery](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1518) during automated discovery to shape follow-on behaviors, including whether or not the adversary fully infects the target and/or attempts specific actions.\n\nSuch software may be deployed widely across the environment for configuration management or security reaso It affects ESXi, IaaS, Linux, macOS, Windows platforms and has been observed used by BRONZE BUTLER, HEXANE, Inception, MuddyWater, Mustang Panda, SideCopy, Sidewinder, Tropic Trooper and malware families such as Bazar, Bundlore, CharmPower, Cobalt Strike, ComRAT, Cuckoo Stealer, Dridex, DustySky. Recommended mitigations include standard security hardening. Detection relies on Application Log Content, Cloud Service Enumeration, Command Execution, Process Creation.",
