    "embedding_text": "Remote Desktop Protocol (T1021.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Lateral Movement tactic. Adversaries may use [Valid Accounts](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1078) to log into a computer using the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP). The adversary may then perform actions as the logged-on user.\n\nRemote desktop is a common feature in operating systems. It allows a user to log into an interactive session with a system desktop graphical user interface on a remote system. Microsoft refers to its implementation of the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) as Remote Desktop Services (RDS).(Citatio It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT1, APT3, APT39, APT41, APT5, Agrius, Akira, Aquatic Panda and malware families such as Carbanak, Cobalt Strike, DarkComet, Pysa, Revenge RAT, SDBbot, ServHelper, WarzoneRAT. Recommended mitigations include Audit, Limit Access to Resource Over Network, Network Segmentation, Operating System Configuration, Disable or Remove Feature or Program. Detection relies on Logon Session Creation, Logon Session Metadata, Network Connection Creation, Process Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may use [Valid Accounts](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1078) to log into a computer using the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP).",
