    "embedding_text": "Office Test (T1137.002) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Persistence tactic. Adversaries may abuse the Microsoft Office \"Office Test\" Registry key to obtain persistence on a compromised system. An Office Test Registry location exists that allows a user to specify an arbitrary DLL that will be executed every time an Office application is started. This Registry key is thought to be used by Microsoft to load DLLs for testing and debugging purposes while developing Office applications. This Registry key is not created by default during an Office installation.(Citation: Hexac It affects Windows, Office Suite platforms and has been observed used by APT28 . Recommended mitigations include Software Configuration, Behavior Prevention on Endpoint. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Creation, Module Load, Process Creation, Windows Registry Key Modification.",
