    "embedding_text": "Application Access Token (T1550.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Lateral Movement tactic. Adversaries may use stolen application access tokens to bypass the typical authentication process and access restricted accounts, information, or services on remote systems. These tokens are typically stolen from users or services and used in lieu of login credentials.\n\nApplication access tokens are used to make authorized API requests on behalf of a user or service and are commonly used to access resources in cloud, container-based applications, and software-as-a-service (SaaS).(Citation: Auth0 It affects Containers, IaaS, Identity Provider, Office Suite, SaaS platforms and has been observed used by APT28, HAFNIUM and malware families such as CreepyDrive, Shai-Hulud. Recommended mitigations include Account Use Policies, Audit, Restrict Web-Based Content, Application Developer Guidance, Encrypt Sensitive Information. Detection relies on User Account Authentication, Web Credential Usage.",
