    "embedding_text": "LSASS Driver (T1547.008) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Persistence, Privilege Escalation tactic. Adversaries may modify or add LSASS drivers to obtain persistence on compromised systems. The Windows security subsystem is a set of components that manage and enforce the security policy for a computer or domain. The Local Security Authority (LSA) is the main component responsible for local security policy and user authentication. The LSA includes multiple dynamic link libraries (DLLs) associated with various other security functions, all of which run in the context of the LSA Subsystem Service It affects Windows platforms and has been observed used by various threat actors and malware families such as Pasam, Wingbird. Recommended mitigations include Privileged Process Integrity, Credential Access Protection, Restrict Library Loading. Detection relies on Driver Load, File Creation, File Modification, Module Load, Windows Registry Key Creation.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may modify or add LSASS drivers to obtain persistence on compromised systems.",
