    "embedding_text": "Environmental Keying (T1480.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may environmentally key payloads or other features of malware to evade defenses and constraint execution to a specific target environment. Environmental keying uses cryptography to constrain execution or actions based on adversary supplied environment specific conditions that are expected to be present on the target. Environmental keying is an implementation of [Execution Guardrails](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1480) that utilizes cryptographic techniques for deriving encryp It affects Linux, Windows, macOS platforms and has been observed used by APT41, Equation and malware families such as InvisiMole, Ninja, PUBLOAD, Pikabot, PowerPunch, ROKRAT, TONESHELL, Winnti for Windows. Recommended mitigations include Do Not Mitigate. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Access, Logon Session Creation, Module Load, Network Connection Creation.",
