    "embedding_text": "Internal Proxy (T1090.001) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Command and Control tactic. Adversaries may use an internal proxy to direct command and control traffic between two or more systems in a compromised environment. Many tools exist that enable traffic redirection through proxies or port redirection, including [HTRAN](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0040), ZXProxy, and ZXPortMap. (Citation: Trend Micro APT Attack Tools) Adversaries use internal proxies to manage command and control communications inside a compromised environment, to reduce the number of simultaneous outbou It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT39, FIN13, Higaisa, Lazarus Group, Lotus Blossom, Strider, Turla, Velvet Ant and malware families such as BACKSPACE, BRICKSTORM, CHOPSTICK, Cobalt Strike, Drovorub, Duqu, FatDuke, GlassWorm. Recommended mitigations include Network Intrusion Prevention. Detection relies on Command Execution, Firewall Rule Modification, Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Content, Network Traffic Flow.",
    "semantic_summary": "Adversaries may use an internal proxy to direct command and control traffic between two or more systems in a compromised environment.",
