    "embedding_text": "Exfiltration Over Unencrypted Non-C2 Protocol (T1048.003) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Exfiltration tactic. Adversaries may steal data by exfiltrating it over an un-encrypted network protocol other than that of the existing command and control channel. The data may also be sent to an alternate network location from the main command and control server.(Citation: copy_cmd_cisco)\n\nAdversaries may opt to obfuscate this data, without the use of encryption, within network protocols that are natively unencrypted (such as HTTP, FTP, or DNS). This may include custom or publicly available encoding/compression a It affects ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT32, APT33, Contagious Interview, FIN6, FIN8, Lazarus Group, Mustang Panda, OilRig and malware families such as Agent Tesla, Brave Prince, CORALDECK, Carbon, CharmPower, Cherry Picker, CookieMiner, CosmicDuke. Recommended mitigations include Network Intrusion Prevention, Data Loss Prevention, Filter Network Traffic, Network Segmentation. Detection relies on Command Execution, File Access, Network Connection Creation, Network Traffic Content, Network Traffic Flow.",
