    "embedding_text": "Local Accounts (T1078.003) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth, Persistence, Privilege Escalation, Initial Access tactic. Adversaries may obtain and abuse credentials of a local account as a means of gaining Initial Access, Persistence, Privilege Escalation, or Defense Evasion. Local accounts are those configured by an organization for use by users, remote support, services, or for administration on a single system or service.\n\nLocal Accounts may also be abused to elevate privileges and harvest credentials through [OS Credential Dumping](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1003). Password reuse may allow the abuse It affects Containers, ESXi, Linux, macOS, Network Devices, Windows platforms and has been observed used by APT29, APT32, FIN10, FIN7, HAFNIUM, Kimsuky, PROMETHIUM, Play and malware families such as Cobalt Strike, Emotet, LockBit 3.0, NotPetya, Umbreon. Recommended mitigations include Privileged Account Management, Multi-factor Authentication, Password Policies, User Account Management. Detection relies on Logon Session Creation, Logon Session Metadata, User Account Authentication.",
