    "embedding_text": "Exploitation for Stealth (T1211) is a MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique in the Stealth tactic. Adversaries may exploit vulnerabilities to evade detection by hiding activity, suppressing logging, or operating within trusted or unmonitored components. \n\nAdversaries may exploit a system or application vulnerability to avoid detection while maintaining access within an environment. Exploitation occurs when an adversary leverages a programming flaw to execute code in a manner that minimizes visibility or blends in with legitimate activity. \n\nRather than directly disabling defenses, adversaries It affects Linux, Windows, macOS, SaaS, IaaS platforms and has been observed used by APT28, Velvet Ant . Recommended mitigations include Exploit Protection, Update Software, Threat Intelligence Program, Application Isolation and Sandboxing. Detection relies on Application Log Content, Module Load, Process Creation.",
